refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;
public RecursiveCachingIteratornullRecursiveCachingIterator::getChildren
Returns the children of the current element, wrapped in a RecursiveCachingIterator that has the same flags. The children are retrieved from the inner iterator when the iterator moves to the element, so the same object is returned until the iterator moves on.

&reftitle.returnvalues;

 The children of the current element, as a
 RecursiveCachingIterator;
 or &null; if the current element has no children.

  &reftitle.examples;

   Iterating over children


<?php
$iterator = new RecursiveCachingIterator(
    new RecursiveArrayIterator(['a' => 1, 'b' => ['c' => 2, 'd' => 3], 'e' => 4]),
    0
);

foreach ($iterator as $key => $value) {
    if (!$iterator->hasChildren()) {
        echo $key, ' = ', $value, "\n";
        continue;
    }

    echo $key, ":\n";
    $children = $iterator->getChildren();
    foreach ($children as $childKey => $childValue) {
        echo '  ', $childKey, ' = ', $childValue, $children->hasNext() ? '' : ' (last)', "\n";
    }
}
?>


   &example.outputs;


a = 1
b:
  c = 2
  d = 3 (last)
e = 4
